* ''The defaults in the decisions row'' (operator, 2026-11-18: //"Approve all the defaults in state/decisions"//; lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/decisions #/ruled-2026-11-18). ''The asked write'' (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/reach-mu #/the-asked-write): T4-1 the AI writes to every wiki the mount reaches below canon on an explicit ask, by the procedure ask, read with the base, `meme_put` with that base, one receipt line naming wiki, layer, bag, acting face and asker; T4-2 canon writes from the AI seat refuse in code as `seat-canon-reach`, after a scratch-house proof; T4-3 a write landing in `personal` reports as a soft miss, never retried elsewhere; T4-4 writes as another face before `C13` refuse by name; T4-5 the chore mark rests in the durable outcome, and one read lists AI writes across wikis; T4-6 the tiddler door for named wikis waits for WAVE TWO after `C13`; T4-7 the AI's reach stays no narrower than the face; T4-8 the MCP tool cards' "lands in its top bag" trues; no lei caps for an asked write within the face's own grants (rank 4k). ''The merge driver'' seats through `lares repo tend` into each clone's shared git config, the pre-commit gate and CI clones reading it absent as fine. ''The old house's burn'': `~/.lares-prior` and `lares-surface:pre-carry` burn after one keep restore drill reads par and no container stands on the image (rank 13b). ''Freyja's collaborator grant'': fork and pull request, no grant, until a Nexus carries canon. ''The rebuild under the pūlama'' (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/rebuild-mu): RD1 one route per rebuild stays until rank 4c lands, then the kūkulu runs routeless with auto-admit closed; RD2 the image builds from the commit, retiring the dirty-tree refusal; RD3 the outgoing image takes a tag by its revision, three stand and the fourth prunes in the same act, and `pulama unadmit` stands; RD4 `up` refuses to recreate a vessel whose image moved without a census; RD5 the kūkulu reads its head by an explicit move; RD6 `vessel rite refresh|rebuild` refuse by name in a container house (rank 4l). ''How the house meets git'' stands ruled as workspaces and read-back by descent (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/decisions #/ruled-workspaces): D7 retires, D8 (promotions onto `refs/house/<face>/canon`) and D10 (`lay --at <commit>`) stand as tools (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/two-hearths-flow #/git-peer-tools). The face-bundle restore keeps its reach across faces, so a pending restore never hides.

